Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P6.32 phase 6: the full-screen map straight from the walking field (field hotkey)

P6.32 phase 6 (docs/P6.32_MAP_ZOOM.md section 18). A key in the walking field, the seventh
binding of the view's table (map_view_field_open, a PS button after the P6.12 / P9.8 map,
default Select), opens the full-screen map without the field menu. The field must stand
still while it is open and come back exactly as it was, so this does not take the status
mode's route (a mode change reloads the stage and rerolls its state): the field is held in
place.

- src/field/field_mode/field.c: in the field task's main state, next to the Start check,
  portFieldMap hands the logical pad and a probe of the field (menuOpen, busy, acting,
  progress, battleSteps, the player's place, the children) to the port. When the port says
  yes (the key went down, map_screen is on, widescreen is on, no other shoulder held, the
  field idle) the field's children are paused with the engine's own task pause (Task.paused:
  a task in TASK_RUN that is paused skips its update and its children, so no actor, event,
  tile stream, script or encounter step runs; the vsync callback and the sequencer go on, so
  the music plays), the Map screen's root is put in children->menu, the slot the Start menu
  uses (the field task already waits in substate 1 until it is NULL and then clears
  menuOpen and busy), and the field task goes to that substate. When the slot is NULL again
  portFieldMapResume unpauses the children and the port gives back what the hold ran on: the
  clocks, the roll sequence, the field's VRAM (the Map screen's images overwrite pages the
  field uses) and the layer scroll.
- src/menus/field_menu/map_screen.c: STSTATUS_createFieldMapRoot, a small root task that
  loads only what the Map screen needs (the sprite sheets and images of the game half, and
  the status sprites the name box frame comes from, to the VRAM places the status mode uses)
  and creates the game's own Map screen, so the cursor, markers, the name box and its text
  are the game's, in whatever language the disc has; the status mode's main task is not used
  (it loads the menu's strings and would show the field menu again at the end). The Map
  screen draws into the field's layer (FIELD_LAYER_MAP) while the session runs, because
  SCREEN_LAYER does not exist in the field. The view opens on that screen by itself; when it
  closes mapViewFrame ends the screen with it, so Triangle returns to the field, not to a
  Map screen.

With the key unbound by an absent option or with map_screen off, widescreen off, a shoulder
button held, the field busy or progress below 4, the poll logs why and nothing else runs:
the field is the one of patch 0140 and the map of 0146 / 0147.

